}

docs {
  # Get Demo Family Tree

  The only tree route that takes no credentials. Returns the tree named by
  `DEMO_TREE_ID`, with `my_permissions` set to the read-only demo capabilities
  (`view`, `view_birth_date`, `view_marriage_date`, `view_photo`).

  Returns `404` when no demo tree is configured, and every request is metered
  per IP by `DEMO_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE`.

  Once you have the id, the ordinary read routes accept it anonymously too —
  `GET /persons?tree_id=…`, `GET /marriages?tree_id=…` and the relation
  endpoints. Write routes still refuse, because the demo grants no write
  capability.

  ## Input
  None.

  ## Output `200`
  ```json
  {
    "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
    "name": "Karimi family",
    "owner_user_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
    "my_permissions": ["view", "view_birth_date", "view_marriage_date", "view_photo"]
  }
  ```
}
